# (#13, 2026-04-22, thirteenth amendment): the 2026-04-22 audit of
# cost-governance surfaced that C14 — the flagship timing-inclusive
# acceptance criterion — was under-tested. C14 packs three
# behaviours into one criterion text (per docs/odd-in-pos.md §5):
# (1) trigger is the prospective-reservation math at activation,
# (2) warning emission precedes the `reservations` row write,
# (3) warning fires exactly once per crossing, not repeatedly per
# debit. The existing test_throttle_warning.py covered (1) and part
# of (3) — fire-once across multiple *reservations* on the same
# crossing — but not the pre-write ordering at all, and not the
# fire-once-across-debits failure mode C14's criterion text names
# explicitly. Amendment #13 adds two new outcome-shaped tests to
# close both gaps. The cost-governance implementation already
# delivers both guarantees structurally — pre-write ordering is
# enforced by the call-site order of `_check_axis` (lines 146-223)
# relative to `store.insert_reservation` (line 233) in ledger.py's
# `reserve_or_refuse`, and fire-once-across-debits is structurally
